# Pop removes and returns the last element

Verifies pop yields the last element of a non-empty int[] array and shortens
the array, leaving the remaining elements in their original order.

>>> source
let values: int[] = [1, 2, 3]
let removed = values->pop()
if (removed != null) {
    print(removed)
}
print(values)

<<< stdout
3
[1, 2]

<<< stderr
